-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f0e830d5-2b3e-4d88-b03e-c6d5247db4d6
-- title:
--   Theorem 4.3 — accumulation points of RSSD along $K$ are stationary, and limiting stationary under gradient sub-consistency (corrected: accumulation points in $\mathcal M$)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $E$ is a finite-dimensional real inner product space (for example $\mathbb R^n$, or a matrix space with $\langle \xi,\eta\rangle=\mathrm{Tr}(\xi^\top\eta)$), $\mathcal M\subseteq E$ is a smooth embedded submanifold, $R$ is a retraction on $\mathcal M$ (Definition 2.1), $f:E\to\mathbb R$ is lower semicontinuous, and $\tilde f$ is a smoothing function of $f$ (Definition 2.7). Let $\{(x_\ell,\mu_\ell,\delta_\ell)\}_{\ell\ge0}$ be the infinite sequence generated by Algorithm 4.1 (RSSD) with $\delta_{opt}=\mu_{opt}=0$ and inputs $x_0\in\mathcal M$, $\delta_0>0$, $\mu_0>0$, $\beta\in(0,1)$, $\bar\alpha>0$, $\theta_\delta,\theta_\mu\in(0,1)$, Armijo constant $\sigma\in(0,1)$, write $\eta_\ell=-\operatorname{grad}\tilde f(x_\ell,\mu_\ell)$, and let
--
--   $$
--   K=\{\ell : \|\eta_\ell\|\le\delta_\ell\}.
--   $$
--
--   Assume Assumption 4.1: for every $\bar\mu>0$ and $\bar x\in\mathcal M$ the level set $\{x\in\mathcal M : \tilde f(x,\bar\mu)\le\tilde f(\bar x,\bar\mu)\}$ is compact.
--
--   Then for every accumulation point $x^*\in\mathcal M$ of $\{x_\ell\}_{\ell\in K}$:
--
--   1. $x^*$ is a stationary point of (1.1) associated with $\tilde f$ on $\mathcal M$ (Definition 3.7), that is,
--   $$
--   \liminf_{x\to x^*,\ x\in\mathcal M,\ \mu\downarrow0}\|\operatorname{grad}\tilde f(x,\mu)\|=0 ;
--   $$
--   2. if, in addition, $\tilde f$ satisfies the Riemannian gradient sub-consistency at $x^*$, i.e. $G_{\tilde f,\mathcal R}(x^*)\subseteq\partial_{\mathcal R}f(x^*)$ (Definition 3.9; in particular if it satisfies it on $\mathcal M$), then $x^*$ is a Riemannian limiting stationary point of (1.1), i.e. $0\in\partial_{\mathcal R}f(x^*)$ (Definition 3.3).
--
--   This is the convergence guarantee of the RSSD method for minimizing a nonsmooth, possibly non-Lipschitz $f$ over a submanifold.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - generalization: M ⊂ ℝⁿ (or a matrix space with ⟨ξ,η⟩ = Tr(ξᵀη)) → M ⊆ E, E any finite-dimensional real inner product space; reason: ℝⁿ and the matrix spaces with the trace inner product are instances, so the Lean statement specializes to the source's
--   - generalization: M a complete Riemannian submanifold embedded in ℝⁿ → M a smooth embedded submanifold of fixed dimension d (C^k coordinate-slice charts for every k), completeness not assumed; reason: completeness is not used in the argument; complete submanifolds are a special case
--   - encoding: f : ℝⁿ → ℝ proper lower semicontinuous → f : E → ℝ with LowerSemicontinuous f; reason: a real-valued function is automatically proper
--   - reading: σ in (4.1) but not on the input line of Algorithm 4.1 → σ ∈ (0,1); reason: the remark on p.15 needs σ < 1, and σ ∈ (0,1) is the Armijo convention of the cited reference [2]
--   - reading: m is the smallest integer such that (4.1) holds → m the least natural number with (4.1); reason: Armijo convention of [2], t_ℓ = β^m ᾱ ≤ ᾱ; over ℤ a least element need not exist
--   - encoding: Algorithm 4.1 with δ_opt = μ_opt = 0, including the stopping test of line 4 → the stopping test is omitted from the run predicate; reason: μ_ℓ > 0 for all ℓ, so the test ‖η_ℓ‖ ≤ 0 and μ_ℓ ≤ 0 never fires and every run is infinite
--   - encoding: accumulation point of {x_ℓ}_{ℓ∈K} → MapClusterPt xstar (atTop ⊓ 𝓟 K) x; reason: cluster point of the subsequence indexed by K, equivalently a limit of x_ℓ along an infinite subset of K
--   - encoding: liminf_{x→x*, x∈M, μ↓0} ‖grad f̃(x, μ)‖ = 0 → 0 is a cluster value of (x, μ) ↦ ‖grad f̃(x, μ)‖ along 𝓝[M] x* ×ˢ 𝓝[>] 0; reason: for a nonnegative function the two are equivalent, and the cluster form has no junk value
--   - encoding: μ_k ↓ 0 in (3.9) → μ_k > 0 and μ_k → 0; reason: the set G_{f̃,R}(x) is the same: pass to a subsequence along which μ_k strictly decreases
--   - generalization: (ii) assumes "f̃ satisfies the Riemannian gradient sub-consistency" (Definition 3.9 defines it at x ∈ M and on M) → sub-consistency only at x*, G_{f̃,R}(x*) ⊆ ∂_R f(x*); reason: the proof uses (3.16) only at x*; sub-consistency on M implies it, so the Lean statement specializes to the source under either reading
--   - reading: h ∈ C¹(B_{x,δ}), with "h ∈ C¹(D) means that h is smooth on D" (p.3) → ContDiffOn ℝ 1 h (closedBall x δ); reason: the C¹ reading of Rockafellar–Wets used by the paper; B_{x,δ} is the closed ball (p.3)
--   - correction: any accumulation point of {x_ℓ}_{ℓ∈K} → any accumulation point lying in M; reason: for a complete but non-closed M the K-iterates can accumulate only outside M, where Definition 3.7 does not apply. Example — E = ℝ², M the spiral r = 1 + 1/θ (θ > 0; complete, embedded, closure ⊇ unit circle C, M ∩ C = ∅), f ≡ 0, f̃(x, μ) = −μ φ((‖x‖² − 1)/(2μ)) with φ(u) = u/(1 + u²) (C^∞, |f̃ − f| ≤ μ/2; on M its values lie in [−μ/2, 0) and tend to 0 at both ends, so Assumption 4.1 holds); with θ_δ < θ_μ², ‖grad f̃(x, μ_ℓ)‖ ≤ δ_ℓ on M forces s = (‖x‖² − 1)/2 = O(μ_ℓ), so the K-iterates approach C; the paper's examples (sphere, Stiefel manifold) are closed and unaffected
-- source:
--   Zhang, Chen & Ma, A Riemannian Smoothing Steepest Descent Method for Non-Lipschitz Optimization on Submanifolds, arXiv:2104.04199v1, Theorem 4.3, p.16

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ProjLikeRetr_Retractor_IsSubmanifold
import Definitions.Def_ZORiem_RGD_rgrad
import Definitions.Def_RiemSmoothSD_IsSmoothRetraction
import Definitions.Def_RiemSmoothSD_IsSmoothingFunction
import Definitions.Def_RiemSmoothSD_RSSDRun
import Definitions.Def_RiemSmoothSD_Subdifferentials
set_option autoImplicit false
open Filter Topology

namespace RiemSmoothSD

open ProjLikeRetr.Retractor ZORiem.RGD

/-- **Theorem 4.3** (Zhang, Chen & Ma, arXiv:2104.04199v1, p.16), corrected to accumulation points
in `M`. Assume Assumption 4.1 holds. Let `K = {ℓ | ‖η_ℓ‖ ≤ δ_ℓ}` and `{x_ℓ}` be an infinite
sequence generated by Algorithm 4.1 with `δ_opt = μ_opt = 0`. Then the following statements hold
for every accumulation point `x* ∈ M` of `{x_ℓ}_{ℓ∈K}`:
(i) `x*` is a stationary point of (1.1) associated with `f̃` on the submanifold `M`
(Definition 3.7);
(ii) in addition, if `f̃` satisfies the Riemannian gradient sub-consistency (Definition 3.9),
then `x*` is a Riemannian limiting stationary point of (1.1) (Definition 3.3).

**Formalization Note** `E` is a finite-dimensional real inner product space (ℝⁿ and matrix
spaces are instances); `M` is a `C^k` coordinate-slice submanifold of dimension `d` for every `k`
(completeness is not assumed); `R : E → E → E` is a retraction in the sense of Definition 2.1
(`IsSmoothRetraction`); `f̃(·, μ)` is `ftilde · μ`; the run `(x_ℓ, μ_ℓ, δ_ℓ)` is `IsRSSDRun` with
the inputs of `RSSDInput` (`σ ∈ (0,1)`); `K = rssdK M ftilde x μ δ`; "`lim_{ℓ→∞, ℓ∈K}`" is the
limit along the filter `atTop ⊓ 𝓟 K`.
"`x*` is an accumulation point of `{x_ℓ}_{ℓ∈K}`" is `MapClusterPt xstar (atTop ⊓ 𝓟 K) x`.
In (ii), sub-consistency is assumed only at `x*` (`RiemGradSubConsistentAt`, (3.16) at `x*`);
sub-consistency on all of `M` (`RiemGradSubConsistent`) implies it, so this covers both readings
of the page's unqualified "satisfies the Riemannian gradient sub-consistency".
The accumulation point is assumed to lie in `M` (correction: for a complete but non-closed `M`,
e.g. a spiral winding onto the unit circle, the accumulation points can all lie outside `M`, where
Definition 3.7 does not apply). -/
theorem theorem_4_3 {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {d : ℕ} {M : Set E} (hM : ∀ k : ℕ, IsSubmanifold k d M)
    {R : E → E → E} (hR : IsSmoothRetraction M R) {f : E → ℝ} (hf : LowerSemicontinuous f)
    {ftilde : E → ℝ → ℝ} (hft : IsSmoothingFunction f ftilde) (hA : Assumption41 M ftilde)
    {x₀ : E} {δ₀ μ₀ β αbar θδ θμ σ : ℝ} (hin : RSSDInput M x₀ δ₀ μ₀ β αbar θδ θμ σ)
    {x : ℕ → E} {μ δ : ℕ → ℝ} (hrun : IsRSSDRun M R ftilde x₀ δ₀ μ₀ β αbar θδ θμ σ x μ δ)
    {xstar : E} (hxM : xstar ∈ M)
    (hacc : MapClusterPt xstar (atTop ⊓ 𝓟 (rssdK M ftilde x μ δ)) x) :
    IsStationaryAssoc M ftilde xstar ∧
      (RiemGradSubConsistentAt M f ftilde xstar → IsLimitingStationary M f xstar) := by sorry

end RiemSmoothSD
